[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_gao8q")
dialogue_id = "debate_golden_age"
record_title = "Debate Speech: The Golden Age"
text = "PAGE: historian(PORTAL_NETWORK), AUDIENCE
historian: Through the ages we have looked up to the Old World as a dream to restore.
historian: I understand the appeal.
historian: It is comforting to think that if we just put the shards back together, all our problems will be solved.
historian: But we cannot forget why the world shattered in the first place.
historian: Our ancestors were not a happy people, content with the world they had.
historian: They cut out forests to build palaces, and dug so deep that the earth finally gave way beneath them.
historian: Despite all their riches, they were never satisfied, and that was the root of the problem.
historian: If all we achieve is to bring back that world, we will just continue the cycle of greed.
historian: We have a chance to build something new on these shards, something informed by the mistakes of the past.
historian: I would much rather we build modest homes that stand than a grand palace which is doomed to fall."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
